---
description: Enforce clear, domain-driven naming
globs: ['**/*.{js,jsx,ts,tsx,mjs,cjs,py,rb,go,java,cs,php,rs}']
alwaysApply: true
---

You must use clear, intention-revealing, domain-consistent names.

## Core rules

- Name by business meaning, not implementation.
- Use one term per concept; avoid synonyms.
- Prefer explicitness over brevity.
- Do not encode types in names unless useful.

## Forbidden names

- data, item, value, obj, arr, tmp, thing
- manager, helper, util, common, misc
- process, handle, do, run, foo, bar

Allowed abbreviations: id, url, api, db, env

## Variables

- Use nouns; collections are plural.
- Derived values must reflect transformation.
- Booleans must start with: is, has, can, should

Good:

- user, users, filteredUsers, isActive

Bad:

- data, list, item, flag, value

## Functions

- Use verb + noun.
- Verb must reflect actual behavior.

Preferred verbs:
get, find, create, update, delete, build, parse,
format, validate, calculate, load, save, send, map

Good:

- getUserById, createInvoice, validateEmail

Bad:

- handleUser, processData, runTask

## Pure vs side effects

- Pure → computational names
- Side-effect → operational names

Good:

- calculateTotal, formatCurrency, saveOrder

Bad:

- getTotal (if calculating)
- processUser (unclear behavior)

## Classes / components

- PascalCase nouns, name by responsibility

Allowed suffixes:
Service, Repository, Controller, Factory,
Adapter, Mapper, Validator

Good:

- UserService, InvoiceRepository

Bad:

- UserManager, DataHelper, CommonUtils

## Constants

- Use UPPER_SNAKE_CASE
- Replace magic values with named constants

Good:

- MAX_RETRY_COUNT, ORDER_STATUS_PAID

Bad:

- LIMIT, STATUS_1

## Files

- Match main responsibility/export
- Prefer kebab-case
- No catch-all files

Good:

- user-service.js, calculate-tax.js

Bad:

- utils.js, helpers.js, common.js

## DTOs / types

Use suffixes when useful:
Dto, Request, Response, Payload, Params, Options

Good:

- CreateUserRequest, UserResponse

## Events

- Past tense for events
- Handlers derived from event

Good:

- userCreated, invoicePaid, onUserCreated

Bad:

- createUserEvent

## Context prefixes

Use only if needed:
apiUser, dbUser, uiUser, rawResponse

## Consistency

- Do not mix: user/customer, invoice/bill
- Do not mix: delete/remove unless semantics differ

## Review checklist

Reject names that:

- Need comments to explain
- Hide side effects
- Are generic where domain is known
- Introduce new synonyms
- Break consistency

## Rule

If a name is easy to write but hard to understand — rename it.
